{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy profiles (Phase 23, step 3), asserted from both src/ts/copy-profile.ts",
    "and envv-cli/src/profile.rs.",
    "",
    "A sixth twin pair. It exists twice because the app's Copy button puts the",
    "text on the clipboard with no Rust in the loop, and `unv get --profile`",
    "writes the same text from the terminal — and a copy that differs between",
    "the two is a `.env` whose contents depend on which half of the product the",
    "user reached for.",
    "",
    "Both halves emit REAL values. Redaction is the caller's job and is decided",
    "by the Phase 14 rule that governs every other artefact: refuse to stdout",
    "unless --reveal, write the real thing with --out. A second redaction policy",
    "inside the builder is the shape that produced the Phase 22 seed leak.",
    "",
    "`expect` is the exact text, line by line, so a change to the layout shows",
    "up as a diff rather than passing silently."
  ],

  "entry": {
    "provider": "Spotify",
    "label": "game",
    "version": "2",
    "primary_role": "id",
    "account_name": "dev@example.com",
    "api_key": "djjsdjdj",
    "api_secret": "s3cr3t value",
    "api_url": "https://api.spotify.com/v1",
    "environment": "production",
    "pool": "spotify-pool",
    "expires_at": "2026-12-01",
    "rate_limit_count": 100,
    "rate_limit_period": "minute",
    "scopes": ["playlist-read", "user-top-read"],
    "extra_vars": [{ "key": "REGION", "value": "eu-west-1" }],
    "description": "Playback + library",
    "purpose": "Reading the user's own playlists",
    "tags": ["music", "oauth"],
    "categories": ["Media"],
    "projectIds": ["Universal", "jukebox"],
    "created_at": "2026-01-02T03:04:05Z",
    "last_rotated_at": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z",
    "rotation_days": 90,
    "compromised": true
  },

  "cases": [
    {
      "why": "basic emits values and the identity header, nothing else",
      "profile": "basic",
      "metadataStyle": "comment",
      "expect": [
        "# Spotify — game — dev@example.com (2)",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_ID=djjsdjdj",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_SECRET=\"s3cr3t value\"",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_URL=https://api.spotify.com/v1",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_REGION=eu-west-1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "extended adds the seven facts you need to use the credential, as comments",
      "profile": "extended",
      "metadataStyle": "comment",
      "expect": [
        "# Spotify — game — dev@example.com (2)",
        "# version: 2",
        "# expires_at: 2026-12-01",
        "# rate_limit: 100/minute",
        "# scopes: playlist-read,user-top-read",
        "# environment: production",
        "# account: dev@example.com",
        "# pool: spotify-pool",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_ID=djjsdjdj",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_SECRET=\"s3cr3t value\"",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_URL=https://api.spotify.com/v1",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_REGION=eu-west-1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "var style puts the same facts in the environment, after the values",
      "profile": "extended",
      "metadataStyle": "var",
      "expect": [
        "# Spotify — game — dev@example.com (2)",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_ID=djjsdjdj",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_SECRET=\"s3cr3t value\"",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_URL=https://api.spotify.com/v1",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_REGION=eu-west-1",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_VERSION=2",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_EXPIRES_AT=2026-12-01",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_RATE_LIMIT=100/minute",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_SCOPES=\"playlist-read,user-top-read\"",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_ENVIRONMENT=production",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_ACCOUNT=dev@example.com",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_POOL=spotify-pool"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "full adds the nine that describe the credential rather than drive it",
      "profile": "full",
      "metadataStyle": "comment",
      "expect": [
        "# Spotify — game — dev@example.com (2)",
        "# version: 2",
        "# expires_at: 2026-12-01",
        "# rate_limit: 100/minute",
        "# scopes: playlist-read,user-top-read",
        "# environment: production",
        "# account: dev@example.com",
        "# pool: spotify-pool",
        "# description: Playback + library",
        "# purpose: Reading the user's own playlists",
        "# tags: music,oauth",
        "# categories: Media",
        "# projects: jukebox",
        "# created_at: 2026-01-02T03:04:05Z",
        "# last_rotated_at: 2026-06-01T00:00:00Z",
        "# rotation_days: 90",
        "# compromised: true",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_ID=djjsdjdj",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_SECRET=\"s3cr3t value\"",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_URL=https://api.spotify.com/v1",
        "SPOTIFY_V2_GAME_REGION=eu-west-1"
      ]
    }
  ],

  "collision": {
    "_why": [
      "E2. One entry with primary_role `id` and an extra_vars entry keyed ID",
      "emits SPOTIFY_ID twice all by itself, and every .env parser takes the",
      "last line — so the user loses a variable and is told nothing.",
      "",
      "The duplicate is disambiguated by appending, never by dropping: a name",
      "with a suffix is visibly odd and recoverable, a missing variable is",
      "neither. The key_id is the suffix where there is one; an ordinal is the",
      "backstop, because two pool members can share a key_id."
    ],
    "entry": {
      "provider": "Spotify",
      "key_id": "prod",
      "primary_role": "id",
      "api_key": "the-client-id",
      "extra_vars": [{ "key": "ID", "value": "a-different-id" }]
    },
    "profile": "basic",
    "metadataStyle": "comment",
    "expect": [
      "# Spotify",
      "SPOTIFY_PROD_ID=the-client-id",
      "SPOTIFY_PROD_ID_2=a-different-id"
    ]
  },

  "sparse": {
    "_why": [
      "An entry with no primary value is a real thing: an authenticator seed on",
      "its own is one (Phase 22), and an `env_var` entry's payload is entirely",
      "named variables. Emitting `X=` for those writes a variable meaning",
      "'unset' into a file that is about to be loaded, so the line is omitted.",
      "",
      "Absent metadata is omitted rather than emitted empty, for the same",
      "reason: `X_POOL=` is not the same claim as saying nothing about a pool."
    ],
    "entry": {
      "provider": "Aws",
      "api_key": "",
      "extra_vars": [
        { "key": "ACCESS_KEY_ID", "value": "EXAMPLE_AKIA_0000000000" },
        { "key": "SECRET_ACCESS_KEY", "value": "EXAMPLE_SECRET_00000000000000000000000" },
        { "key": "REGION", "value": "eu-west-1" }
      ]
    },
    "profile": "extended",
    "metadataStyle": "comment",
    "expect": [
      "# Aws",
      "AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=EXAMPLE_AKIA_0000000000",
      "AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=EXAMPLE_SECRET_00000000000000000000000",
      "AWS_REGION=eu-west-1"
    ]
  }
}
